A presentation should adapt to the conversation, not force the conversation to adapt to the presentation.

Giving AI the ability to navigate existing material contextually is an interesting step toward more natural knowledge sharing.

@tavus partner.

@tavus One aspect that caught my attention is the shift from presenting slides to presenting knowledge.

A traditional deck follows a predefined sequence, while a conversational presentation can adapt to the questions being asked and bring the right information into the discussion at the right moment.

That has the potential to make presentations more useful, especially when the goal is understanding rather than simply delivering content.

